  "_comment": "Curated raw-material purchase manifest for scripts/whistlebird_migration.py. 'clean' records are real order-confirmation emails, imported as dated receipts without allocation to a specific consuming batch (same policy as legacy raw materials, WB-018): botanicals from jill@alembics.co.nz (post-legacy-cutoff, 2025-05-13 onward) and, since 2026-09-18, every Neutral grain spirit receipt ever bought from spirits@southerngrainspirits.co.nz (2023-04-24 onward -- superseding the legacy purchases_gns table as the sole NGS source; see whistlebird_replay_timeline._ngs_allocations, which pools these instead of reading purchases_gns, so the replay no longer needs legacy-DB access for NGS). 'resolved_by_context' records have no email or database purchase evidence. Since 2026-09-19 they are modelled restocks of one whole real pack (`restock_packs`: the size the botanical is actually bought in), bought only when stock runs out, dated 3 days before the maceration that first needed it (`first_needed_by`), and NOT pinned to that batch -- every later batch draws the same lot down FIFO, so one purchase fans out across all the batches it feeds. They are generated by `scripts/whistlebird_replay_simulation.py plan --write` (which rebuilds every record of that kind from scratch) and are never sized to a single batch's use. The only exact-quantity `consumed_by` records left are the three VAT59 supplier lots, which are real receipts (`purchase_quantity`); where a later physical lot label establishes the full receipt, `purchase_quantity` is the quantity created in inventory while `quantity` remains the exact amount consumed by the named VAT. Supplier per the founder's 2026-09-14 supplier list (updated same day to add Szechuan pepper -> Davis Trading and Green tea -> Countdown/Woolworths), not verified against a receipt. Founder-confirmed 2026-09-14: each distillation runs two multi-shot concentrates into one VAT, so real per-batch consumption is 2x the founder's stated per-shot 